mmcefs - status, testing and notes
==================================

User documentation (mount options, limitations, messages):
Documentation/filesystems/mmcefs.txt

Status
------

  - Builds with the PS2 toolchain (gcc 2.95.2) as a module or built-in
    (`CONFIG_MMCEFS=y`), without warnings.
  - WORKING AND VERIFIED ON PSBBN HARDWARE (2026-11-08, SCPH-70008 with
    SD2PSX in slot 0, kernel commit 8eeec6e):
    * Automatic on-mount IRX loading (`iomanX.irx`, `fileXio.irx`,
      `mmceman.irx`) from `/lib/modules/irx/` via runtime SBV patches in
      `arch/mips/ps2/loadfile.c`.
    * Full VFS operations verified on real hardware: directory listing,
      subdirectory traversal, file reading, file creation/writing, and
      unlink/deletion.
    * Full coexistence with DualShock controller (`PADMAN` / `ps2pad`) and
      Memory Card manager (`MCMAN` / `[ps2mc]` thread in `SW` state, BBN
      Memory Card utility working normally).

Pieces
------

  arch/mips/ps2/loadfile.c   ps2_load_module_buffer(): copies an IRX to the
                             IOP heap (SIF DMA) and starts it through the
                             LOADFILE RPC service (0x80000006, function 6).
  fs/mmcefs/fxio.c           fileXio RPC client (service 0x0b0b0b00).
  fs/mmcefs/super.c          mount, options, IRX loading, inodes.
  fs/mmcefs/namei.c          lookup/create/mkdir/unlink/rmdir/rename/readdir.
  fs/mmcefs/file.c           page cache I/O over one IOP fd per inode.
  fs/mmcefs/irx/             iomanX.irx, fileXio.irx (ps2sdk v2.0.0),
                             mmceman.irx (ps2-mmce release), with licenses.

Testing on the PS2
------------------

Build the kernel and modules as in the top-level README.md (the IRX files
are copied to rootfs/lib/modules/irx), install them, boot, then:

  dmesg -c > /dev/null
  insmod mmcefs                  # or modprobe mmcefs
  mkdir -p /mnt/mmce
  mount -t mmcefs -o slot=0 none /mnt/mmce
  dmesg                          # expect "mmcefs: loaded ..." x3
  ls -la /mnt/mmce

Then, step by step (stop at the first failure and keep dmesg):

  1. cat a small text file from the card; md5sum a large one and compare
     with the same file read on a PC.
  2. cp a file >8 KB to the card, sync, umount, mount again, md5sum it.
  3. mkdir /mnt/mmce/test; touch, echo >>, rm, rmdir inside it.
  4. ls a directory with many files (e.g. the card's MemoryCards folder).
  5. umount, mount again with slot=1 if a second MMCE is present.
  6. After everything, check the SD card on a PC (chkdsk/fsck).

Things to report back if it fails: full dmesg, the step, the exact error.

Hardware findings (2026-11-01 .. 2026-11-08)
--------------------------------------------

  1. PSBBN LOADFILE & MODLOAD runtime SBV patches (`arch/mips/ps2/loadfile.c`):
     - PSBBN's IOP has a stock LOADFILE server which originally served only
       function 0 (`LF_F_MOD_LOAD`) and rejected unsigned `mc0:` paths (-201).
     - `ps2_sbv_patch_enable_lmb()` patches the LOADFILE RPC jump table to
       support function 6 (`LF_F_MOD_BUF_LOAD`), enabling `ps2_load_module_buffer()`
       to dynamically load `iomanX.irx`, `fileXio.irx`, and `mmceman.irx` from
       EE memory buffers without modifying `BB.ELF`.
     - `ps2_sbv_patch_disable_prefix_check()` disables the MODLOAD path check.
     - Fixed an adjacent instruction overwrite in `loadfile.c` (commit `8eeec6e`)
       that previously triggered an Reserved Instruction Exception (`0x00000028`)
       in `LOADFILE` on the IOP.

  2. PSBBN IOP runtime (`IOPRP 2.4.x` / `MODLOAD 1.5`) compatibility fixes in
     `iomanX.irx` and `mmceman.irx`:
     - Module import table versions: downgraded `intrman` import table version in
       `iomanX.irx` (`0x0102` -> `0x0101`), and downgraded `loadcore` (`0x0103`
       -> `0x0101`) and `intrman` (`0x0102` -> `0x0101`) in `mmceman.irx`.
     - `MODLOAD 1.5` `_start` ABI: `MODLOAD 1.5` passes only `(argc, argv)` to
       `_start` (not `ModuleInfo *mi` in `$a2`), so `_start` in `iomanX.irx` and
       `mmceman.irx` was patched to skip `mi` dereference and return `0`
       (`MODULE_RESIDENT_END`).
     - Eliminated `intrman` export 15 (`GetIntrmanInternalData`) dependency in
       `mmceman.irx`: instead of hijacking `IRQ 17` (`INTR_SIO2`) via
       `GetIntrmanInternalData()`, `mmceman` uses polled SIO2 completion
       (`my_wait_sio2_complete` at `0x0530`, polling `0xbf80826c` bit 12
       `TR_IDLE` with `0x0a1` transfer start and `0x0ac` FIFO reset), and
       restores `0xbf808268 = 0x03bc` (re-enabling `0x300` IRQ bits for
       `sio2man`) in `mmce_sio2_unlock`.

  3. Upstream bugs discovered and fixed in `mmceman.irx` (applicable to upstream
     `ps2-mmce/mmceman`):
     - SIO2 Transfer Queue Contamination (`0xbf808200..0xbf80823c`):
       `MCMAN` and `PADMAN` populate multiple entries in the 16-register SIO2
       transfer queue (`SIO2_REG_BASE[0..15]`), whereas `mmceman` only writes
       `SIO2_REG_BASE[0]`. Without zeroing `SIO2_REG_BASE[1..15]`, the SIO2
       controller chains into stale `MCMAN`/`PADMAN` descriptors after the first
       MMCE packet, sending stray clocks and desynchronizing the SD2PSX RP2040
       PIO state machine on multi-packet commands (`dread`, `open`, `read`,
       `write`). Added `clear_sio2_queue_and_settle` (`0x0688`) to zero all 16
       registers and wait ~15us for the RP2040 `/CS` rising-edge PIO reset.
     - `sio2man` Mutex Hook & `PADMAN` Event Flag Collision (`_sio2man_hook`):
       Upstream `mmceman` only accepted `sio2man` versions `0x201` and `0x207`
       (rejecting PSBBN's `sio2man v2.3` = `0x203` with 61 exports) and hooked
       export 23 (`sio2_pad_transfer_init`), which uses `sio2_ef` event bits
       `0x001`/`0x002` — colliding directly with `PADMAN`'s 60Hz VBlank thread!
       Patched `_sio2man_hook` (`0x0304..0x0338`, respecting MIPS I R3000A load
       delay slots) to accept any `sio2man` with `>= 51` exports and use export
       50 (`sio2_mc2_transfer_init`, dedicated event bits `0x100`/`0x200`) for
       locking and export 26 (`sio2_transfer_reset`, bit `0x1000`) for unlocking.
     - VFS Return Values in `mmce_fs_dread` and `mmce_fs_getstat`:
       * `mmce_fs_dread`: upstream returned `-1` on end-of-directory (`rdbuf[4]
         != 0`) instead of `0`, and returned `rdbuf[1]` (`0x00` reserved byte)
         on entry success instead of `1` (`> 0`). Fixed to return `1` on entry
         read and `0` on end-of-directory (with proper `mmce_sio2_unlock`).
       * `mmce_fs_getstat`: upstream returned `-1` (`-EPERM`) when a file did
         not exist (`rdbuf[0x29] != 0`), breaking VFS negative lookups and file
         creation (`O_CREAT`). Fixed to return `-2` (`-ENOENT`).

Known risks (check these first)
-------------------------------

  - "LOADFILE RPC service not available": PSBBN's IOP runtime has no
    LOADFILE server.  Then the modules have to be loaded before Linux
    starts (and mount with -o noload), or another loading path is needed.
  - "loading ... failed" / "did not stay resident": IOP module load error
    or the module refused to start.  For mmceman this usually means it
    could not hook sio2man (it needs sio2man >= 1.2; PSBBN's version is
    unknown).
  - "fileXio RPC service not available": fileXio.irx did not start
    (iomanX missing or failed).
  - "no mmce0: device": mmceman is not running or no MMCE answered in
    that slot.
  - Hangs or wrong data: suspect the DMA path in fxio.c - physical
    addresses (virt_to_phys) and dma_cache_wback_inv/dma_cache_inv around
    each transfer, and the "rests" handling in fx_read().

Notes for agents
----------------

  - Locking: fx_lock() serialises all RPCs, guards the shared DMA buffers
    and the per-inode IOP fds, and keeps seek+read/write atomic.  It nests
    inside the page lock and i_sem.  Never call filldir(), copy_*_user()
    or allocate with __GFP_FS while holding it.
  - Everything the IOP DMAs into or out of (and the RPC client data the
    SBIOS updates) must be in KSEG0 memory from the page allocator: a
    module's static data is in vmalloc space and virt_to_phys() is wrong
    there.  See struct fx_bufs in fxio.c.
  - iomanX returns newlib errno numbers; fx_errno() maps the ones that
    differ from Linux (ENOTEMPTY 90, ENAMETOOLONG 91, ENOTSUP 134, ...).
  - mmceman has no rename, chstat (times/modes) or sync; mmcefs_rename()
    removes an existing target only after the device answered EEXIST, so
    an unsupported rename never deletes data.
  - Do not reintroduce a block device for the SD card: the MMCE protocol
    has no raw sector access (only file commands, see docs in
    github.com/ps2-mmce/mmceman).
  - When updating the IRX files, update the sha256 list in irx/README.
